  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Justice Co-financing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">State and non-state justice providers, oversight actors, media and the public will develop &#x2018;common principles&#x2019; of inclusive and accountable justice provision and a roadmap for inclusive justice. Inclusive justice facilitation groups in districts and Kathmandu will facilitate dialogue, undertake and inform advocacy, and monitor and oversee the inclusive, effective and accountable provision of state and non-state justice.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target Groups: The project systematically addresses CIT-companies and investors within Afghanistan and those with activities in Afghanistan from the regional level, especially in Pakistan. Within Afghanistan, small and medium private companies of several regional hubs of the CIT-sector will be chosen in Kabul, Herat, Mazar-i Sharif. Joint ventures as well as Afghan companies will be addressed. Stakeholders: International donors and development agencies (World Bank, ADB, etc.), government institutions, private investors are stakeholders who define development and investment policy in the CIT-sector. They will be involved in the project.Lobby groups (e.g. trade unions, chamber of commerce), security actors (e.g. police, militias, gangs), local communities, vulnerable groups, patronage networks will be considered.Attention will be taken about the social, ethnic, regional balance in employment, conflict settings, and agenda setting by influential actors.</narrative>
  </description>
